      "IsMRef": true,
      "Title": "MewExtendedToolkit.Html.HtmlContainer",
      "Summary": "<p sourcefile=\"api/MewExtendedToolkit.Html.HtmlContainer.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"1\">Low level handling of Html Renderer logic, this class is used by <xref href=\"MewExtendedToolkit.Html.HtmlLabel\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref> and <xref href=\"MewExtendedToolkit.Html.HtmlPanel\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref>.</p>\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "ManagedReference",
      "source_relative_path": "api/MewExtendedToolkit.Html.HtmlControl.yml",
      "output": {
        ".html": {
          "relative_path": "api/MewExtendedToolkit.Html.HtmlControl.html"
        }
      },
      "version": "",
      "Uid": null,
      "IsMRef": true,
      "Title": "MewExtendedToolkit.Html.HtmlControl",
      "Summary": "<p sourcefile=\"api/MewExtendedToolkit.Html.HtmlControl.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"1\">Provides HTML rendering using the text property.<br>\nMewUI control that will render html content in it's client rectangle.<br>\nThe control will handle mouse and keyboard events on it to support html text selection, copy-paste and mouse clicks.<br></p>\n<p>\nThe major differential to use HtmlPanel or HtmlLabel is size and scrollbars.<br>\nIf the size of the control depends on the html content the HtmlLabel should be used.<br>\nIf the size is set by some kind of layout then HtmlPanel is more suitable, also shows scrollbars if the html contents is larger than the control client rectangle.<br>\n</p>\n<p>\n<h4>LinkClicked event:</h4>\nRaised when the user clicks on a link in the html.<br>\nAllows canceling the execution of the link.\n\n<p>\n<h4>StylesheetLoad event:</h4>\nRaised when a stylesheet is about to be loaded by file path or URI by link element.<br>\nThis event allows to provide the stylesheet manually or provide new source (file or uri) to load from.<br>\nIf no alternative data is provided the original source will be used.<br>\n\n<p>\n<h4>ImageLoad event:</h4>\nRaised when an image is about to be loaded by file path or URI.<br>\nThis event allows to provide the image manually, if not handled the image will be loaded from file or download from URI.\n\n<p>\n<h4>RenderError event:</h4>\nRaised when an error occurred during html rendering.<br>\n\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "ManagedReference",
      "source_relative_path": "api/MewExtendedToolkit.Html.HtmlLabel.yml",
      "output": {
        ".html": {
          "relative_path": "api/MewExtendedToolkit.Html.HtmlLabel.html"
        }
      },
      "version": "",
      "Uid": null,
      "IsMRef": true,
      "Title": "MewExtendedToolkit.Html.HtmlLabel",
      "Summary": "<p sourcefile=\"api/MewExtendedToolkit.Html.HtmlLabel.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"1\">Provides HTML rendering using the text property.<br>\nMewUI control that will render html content in it's client rectangle.<br>\nUsing <xref href=\"MewExtendedToolkit.Html.HtmlLabel.AutoSize\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref> and <xref href=\"MewExtendedToolkit.Html.HtmlLabel.AutoSizeHeightOnly\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref> client can control how the html content effects the\nsize of the label. Either case scrollbars are never shown and html content outside of client bounds will be clipped.\nMaxWidth/MaxHeight and MinWidth/MinHeight with AutoSize can limit the max/min size of the control<br>\nThe control will handle mouse and keyboard events on it to support html text selection, copy-paste and mouse clicks.<br></p>\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "ManagedReference",
      "source_relative_path": "api/MewExtendedToolkit.Html.HtmlPanel.yml",
      "output": {
        ".html": {
          "relative_path": "api/MewExtendedToolkit.Html.HtmlPanel.html"
        }
      },
      "version": "",
      "Uid": null,
      "IsMRef": true,
      "Title": "MewExtendedToolkit.Html.HtmlPanel",
      "Summary": "<p sourcefile=\"api/MewExtendedToolkit.Html.HtmlPanel.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"1\">Provides HTML rendering using the text property.<br>\nMewUI control that will render html content in it's client rectangle.<br>\nIf the layout of the html resulted in its content beyond the client bounds of the panel it will show scrollbars (horizontal/vertical) allowing to scroll the content.<br>\nThe control will handle mouse and keyboard events on it to support html text selection, copy-paste and mouse clicks.<br></p>\n"
    },
